+# Flight 93 boarding-pass and ticket-coupon record
+
+November 14, 2026 UTC · TEL01–TEL04 / AUD016-A1. A newly inspected FBI report supplies an evidence-custody lead for travel records relevant to the [unresolved report 6390 itinerary wording](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/a9b917df176d022ab2b19b7fb785ceddd1bffd4b/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-glick-6390-first-report-2026-11-14/README.md). The actual boarding passes, ticket coupons, booking history and custody disposition were not acquired.
+
+## What the records describe
+
+| Source | Observation |
+| --- | --- |
+| **FBI report NK-744**, Commission Team 7 Box 12 item 415, physical p. 1 | An airline employee is reported to have supplied **38 boarding passes** on September 11, 2001, described as used by passengers boarding Flight 93 at **Gate 17, Terminal A, Newark**. The typed list includes **Jeremy Glick**. The form records investigation **09/11/2001** and dictation and transcription **09/12/2001**. The sheet has later handwritten markings; their authorship, purpose and timing are not established here. |
+| **Same report**, physical p. 2 | A separate numbered item describes **40 airline ticket coupons and discarded ticket parts from various flights**. The report says the items were being maintained as evidence at the FBI's Newark office. It does not identify the coupon holders or flight dates in that description, and it does not establish the items' later disposition. |
+| [National Park Service Flight 93 timeline](https://www.nps.gov/flni/learn/historyculture/september-11-2001-timeline.htm) | Its introductory flight summary gives **37 passengers and 7 crew**, Newark to San Francisco; its boarding section describes Gate 17 and a planned non-stop trip. This is a historical reconstruction, not the boarding passes or carrier manifest. |
+
+The report's **38 boarding passes** and the NPS's **37 passengers** are distinct reported counts attached to different descriptions. Their respective populations and inclusion rules have not been established; retain both. The separate **40 coupons** are described as from various flights, and must not be counted as Flight 93 passengers, independent confirmation, or evidence that a particular passenger's September 10 ticket survives. A proper comparison needs the underlying passes, passenger/crew manifest and source-to-list accounting.
+
+## Relevance to the itinerary question
+
+The released [September 12 interview copy on the FBI Vault, physical p. 13](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-01-of-08/at_download/file#page=13), describes intended September 10 travel delayed after a Newark airport fire, and Flight 93 on September 11 as en route **non-stop** to San Francisco. The earlier [report 6390](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/a9b917df176d022ab2b19b7fb785ceddd1bffd4b/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-glick-6390-first-report-2026-11-14/README.md) attributes a **Cincinnati detour** to a Newark–San Francisco flight in an agent-sourced account. Keep the differing words and source chains intact; the acquired records do not establish what flight or date that reference meant, or why the accounts differ.
+
+The Vault page and the previously examined 11722 Commission copy represent the same interview account and must not be counted as independent corroboration. The Box 12 boarding-pass report is a separate FBI report about airline-supplied materials; the underlying passes and their itinerary fields have not been inspected. Neither it nor the NPS summary establishes that the 40 coupon items include a September 10 booking or a Cincinnati leg.
+
+## Exact retrieval targets
+
+- [ ] Locate the **NK-744 / M-INT-00021713** evidence inventory, item identifiers, 38 boarding passes, and 40-coupon collection, including retention, transfers and disposition. Verify whether any coupon concerns the relevant individual or September 10 travel before using it for that purpose.
+- [ ] Obtain the relevant airline reservation, rebooking and passenger itinerary history, original 6390 notes and 11722 source notes. Seek independent flight-operation records as well; keep any different travel dates and flights separate.
+- [ ] Preserve the unresolved **38 boarding-pass / 37 passenger** descriptions and identify each source's scope before attempting a count comparison. No cause, actor intent or missing-person inference follows from these aggregate labels.
+
+## Source and verification scope
+
+The Commission archive member was retrieved by HTTP byte range with ZIP-header, member-name, ETag, size and CRC checks. Its two pages were visually inspected; the analysis above uses the stated evidence categories and the one named traveler, not the other listed individuals. The held FBI Vault PDF was rehashed and physical p. 13 visually checked; its prior Commission copy and 6390 remain separately preserved. The NPS timeline's displayed text was acquired and hashed. No image or underlying personal details were published. [Source pins](SOURCE-PINS.json).
